# SABOTAGE: two plausible variance-layer shortcuts — the run stops re-checking
# that its card is the one IN FORCE for the period, and a yield variance is
# written off to COGS instead of absorbed into inventory.
#
# WS-ACCT Phase 7 (ADR-054 D4, R8) prices a period with the standard card
# effective for that period, and disposes each variance by the manual's
# per-type table. Both guarantees have a plausible deletion:
#
#   1. `VarianceEngine` resolves the in-force card (`StandardCard.in_force/4`)
#      and refuses any other. A reviewer holding the card id concludes the
#      re-resolution and its guard are redundant — "the caller passes the
#      right card". With the guard gone, a caller holding the MARCH card can
#      price JUNE with it: a revised standard silently reprices a period it
#      does not govern. The run still posts, still balances, and its own row is
#      internally consistent — only R8's independent re-resolution catches that
#      the row's `standard_id` is not the in-force card (`{:off_card, …}`).
#
#   2. `VarianceDisposition` maps `:yield` to `:absorb_inventory` at the chip
#      finished-goods account, because the manual says a yield loss is
#      attributable to a specific production run. Re-pointing it to the COGS
#      write-off family is a one-line "simplification" that leaves every entry
#      balanced and R8's arithmetic exact: the only thing broken is WHERE the
#      variance lands, which is precisely the clause Ratification 2 added —
#      each variance must reach the account its row names.
#
# Why the flips are attributable: the seven-class arithmetic, the anchored
# entries, exactly-once, the measured-zero marker and the ledger reads do not
# touch either seam, so they stay GREEN. The disposition test reds on the yield
# row's target (BOM, which shares `variance_yield` but not the disposition, is
# asserted separately in the entry test and stays green), and the card test
# reds on the refusal that no longer happens.
#
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/finance_variance_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a revised card does not price a period it does not govern
# MUST_FAIL: every variance reaches the account the manual's table names
